[[3629,1369,"the night concierge who found Ms Atshiki had not had any first aid training from St Mungo's","lack of first aid training for night concierge",""],[3630,1369,"the hostel does stock naloxone (used in the emergency treatment of opiate/opioid toxicity), but that the night concierge is not trained in its use","lack of naloxone training for night concierge",""],[3631,1369,"there are only ever two members of staff working at the hostel at night, of which the night concierge is one","insufficient night staffing at hostel",""],[3632,1369,"Nobody at the hostel attempted to perform cardiopulmonary resuscitation on Ms Atshiki","no CPR attempted on deceased",""],[3633,1369,"the night concierge stayed with her as she lay across the stairs, while the other member of staff stayed by the front door to open it when the ambulance service arrived","staff positioned away from medical emergency location",""]]